  "title": "Driving and delivery",
  "level": "A2–B1",
  "reviewed": false,
  "_note": "portuguese-for-work run, 2026-11-22: written by hand for Portugal (European Portuguese, pt-PT), not yet read by a human. translations.en = English meaning; deHint = German translation (the 'German' tab). Words already in the lexicon, the IMT deck or another sector are refs, with this job's own example and sense. Working conditions, contracts and rules are general orientation only.",
  "intro": "Driving is a common way into work in Portugal: TVDE (ride-hailing apps), food and parcel delivery (the estafetas), and vans and lorries for distribution companies. This deck has the vehicle, your daily work, routes and deliveries, rules and safety, and what you say at the door and to your team. Customers get the third person: «Boa tarde, trago uma encomenda para a Sra. Costa.» For the licence and the road itself, see the IMT vocabulary.",
  "introEasy": "Do you drive or deliver in Portugal? Learn the words for your work here.",
  "jobs": [
    "Motorista de TVDE",
    "Estafeta",
    "Motorista de distribuição",
    "Motorista de pesados",
    "Ajudante de motorista"
  ],
  "tipps": [
    "Driving for TVDE needs more than a driving licence: a TVDE driver certificate (with a training course) and a TVDE operator (operador) to drive for. The rules have changed several times; check the current ones with the IMT before you start. General orientation, not legal advice.",
    "Many estafetas and TVDE drivers work as trabalhador independente and issue recibos verdes on the Portal das Finanças, with their own Social Security contributions. Ask an accountant (contabilista) how this works for you.",
    "At the door: greet, say what you bring and ask for a signature or a code: «Boa tarde, trago uma encomenda para a Sra. Costa. Pode assinar aqui?»"
  ],
